rca_of_the_issue:
Reproduction: open /new, enter any thesis, click 'Draft the rules'. Observed: button goes blue briefly, SSE POST to /api/relay/ai/generate/stream returns 200 (via relay), body contains upstream JSON `{"error":"You’ve drafted 5 strategies today…"}`. Root cause: (1) backend relay for /stream always returns 200 with media_type=text/event-stream regardless of upstream status — see server.py lines 49-59 — and does not reframe non-SSE error bodies as `event: error` frames. (2) frontend sseStream in /lib/api.js parses only well-formed SSE events so the error JSON is dropped. (3) New.jsx fallback calls weft.generate() which 429s again; errorMessage(e2).toast call ran but no DOM error element was observed. Mitigation: in server.py, after opening the upstream stream check `r.status_code` and `r.headers['content-type']`; if not SSE, read body and yield `event: error
data: {…}

`, OR return a non-streaming Response that propagates upstream status. Additionally in New.jsx catch block, show an inline banner so toast isn't the only surface.
